From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:34:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 014/148] [ae-patch] Take the slot limit from the server's
 capacity answer

The slot cap became one setting in omnigent-ae on 2026-09-24: AE_SLOT_LIMIT in
config/server.env, reported as `limit` by GET /v1/ae/capacity. The web UI still
counted against a constant 3 in the sidebar's Dashboard row (patch 0001), the
session header chip (0007) and the Status submenu's fallback (0004), so a
server set to four slots would have shown 3/3 in red while the cap let a
fourth through.

New file web/src/lib/aeSlotLimit.ts: useAeSlotLimit reads `limit` from the
capacity route through the query cache (once per load, stale after five
minutes, no retry), with AE_SLOT_LIMIT from aeLabels as the fallback until it
answers or when it cannot. The Status submenu keeps the limit each capacity
answer carries, so the counts repaint with it, and its sidebar fallback uses
the last limit the server gave. The refusal toast says "one more" instead of
"a fourth".

Only AE files change; no upstream file is touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
